1. create a new repository on the command line
echo "# Git.Common" >> README.md
git init: => Init git
git add README.md => add a file
git commit -m "first commit" => Commit
git branch -M main 
git remote add origin https://github.com/DHA1985/Git.Common.git
git push -u origin main

2. push an existing repository from the command line
git remote add origin https://github.com/YorGithub/Git.Common.git
git branch -M main
git push -u origin main

3. Rename branch
- From master to main
git branch -m master main

4. Push to GitHub
git push -u origin main

5. Delete old branch not in use in github

git push origin --delete master

5. Kiem tra status tai repo
git branch -a
git remote -v
git status
